{
	title: 'Buffer Anthropic tool inputs before execution',
	spec: 'Anthropic requests use ordinary buffered tool-input streaming, not the legacy global fine-grained streaming beta. Hal executes tool calls only after complete input is parsed, so buffering preserves the invariant that unvalidated fragments never run and avoids foregoing provider JSON validation without using early fragments. OAuth identity and required beta headers remain intact; API-key requests omit unnecessary beta headers. Local argument validation, full malformed-input errors, truncated-input handling, cancellation, and file-change snapshots remain unchanged. Provider tests exercise both authentication routes and existing malformed/truncated streams.',
	status: 'done',
